WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Henry Winkler.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.067
We've talked in the past.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.501
I think anyone who follows you
on social media

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.167
knows you are an avid fisherman.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.367
-I am.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.734
-And Stacey, your wife --
-Is better than I am.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:11.934
-Is she better than you?

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.400
-The last time we went,
this past September,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.601
her fish were bigger.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:16.868
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:20.000
And I don't know --
We were using the same fly.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.133
I don't know how it happened.
-Gotcha.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.300
Were you celebratory
of her success?

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.400
-Well, outside I was.
-Yeah? Oh, that's good.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.767
That's all anyone
can ask from a spouse.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.167
You don't have to
believe a thing.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.801
You just have to
show it in public.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:36.501
-Just, "Oh, my!
That is phenomenal!"

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:39.701
-"I'm going to go
stand by this tree

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.734
and face away from you now."

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.701
-That's why we fish
in different boats.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.133
-Oh, that's very smart.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.968
-So I don't have to experience

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:51.000
her pulling out
these beautiful trout

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.267
and mine are just "tr."

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.300
-You went to Yale Drama School.
-I did.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.968
-Can I show my favorite photo
from the book?

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.868
-Sure.
-Because it just --

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.767
I can't even believe
this was you.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.334
Check out young Henry there.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.100
Like, who --
[ Audience "oohs" ]

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.167
Yeah, that is absolutely
the appropriate response.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.133
-I thought that was going to be
my first headshot.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.934
-That is --
What roles did you want?

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:18.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:21.667
You were like, "I'm a biker
and also a fisherman."

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.267
-Yes, and I wanted --
I wanted to play an Irishman.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.267
-Yeah. You did.
I mean, it's so funny.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.767
I mean, I guess
if you were the Fonz,

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:29.968
you could have been
an Irishman, too.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.234
I mean, you might as well,
right?

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.834
-Really.
-You could have done them all.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.067
I also want to ask --

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:37.400
So you grew up
and you wrote a series of books,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.701
"Hank Zipzer."
-Yes.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.133
-And these are children's books
about the fact

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.801
that you had dyslexia
when you were young.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.767
And these are books
for young readers.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:50.501
-Right, and I understood now

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:54.300
what it was like to be 8
and to fail

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.667
and to understand now

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.701
that no matter how difficult
it is to learn,

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:04.667
no matter how difficult it is
for you to be in school,

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:09.267
it has nothing to do with who
you are or how smart you are.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.367
-That's a lovely message
for kids.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.968
How many of the Zipzer books
have you written now?

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:16.934
-There are 28 Hank Zip--

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:21.334
Now, the the newest one
is "Detective Duck,"

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:23.467
and she just came out
14 days ago.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.734
-Wow, look at this.
Two books in 14 days.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.133
-It's unbelievable.
-Unbelievable.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:30.300
-With Lin Oliver.
And she is a little duckling.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.000
She lives on a pond,
the picture of which I found

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.634
when we were doing a jigsaw
puzzle over the pandemic.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.767
-Yeah.
-And there was a picture

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.834
of a pond in New Hampshire,

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.601
and we said,
"That's where the duck lives."

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.033
-Wow! So the thing

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.601
that was stopping you
from writing this book

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.801
was you didn't know
what the pond looked like?

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:54.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.634
-I was torn.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.067
You probably had a bunch
of ponds to choose --

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:04.701
-There was a pond
in Winston-Salem.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.200
-Sure.
-But not as good-looking.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.901
-Yeah. I mean, I bet
there were a lot of people

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.467
who were sending you
pictures of their ponds.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.567
-And you know what?

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.167
And I have to say,
they weren't great.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.567
-Yeah.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:17.834
-I got a lot
of bad pictures of ponds.

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.200
-When you go over
to your house now,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.133
you got photo albums
full of your bad ponds.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.300
-Really.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.767
-I've put them in a shed.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.767
-Yeah, well,
as a kid with dyslexia,

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.200
do you ever look back and go,

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.801
"Oh, my God, look at all
these books that I've written"?

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:36.534
-When I see my name on a book,
I am telling you I am --

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:40.100
I was 78 two days ago, and --

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.934
And everything about me is young

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:51.868
except for my knees
when I stand up.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:56.968
But anyway, when I see my name
on a book, it is --

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:59.334
I'm overwhelmed.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.601
When I saw my name
the first time,

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:05.367
I'm at a meeting
and I'm talking to the buyers

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:08.234
all across the country of books.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:12.334
And I look down, and there is
my name on a book

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:16.501
as a part of a writing team.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.868
My brain turned to cream cheese.

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.033
Literally, I stopped talking.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:24.501
I picked up the book
off the table.

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:27.300
I rubbed it all over my body.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:34.133
I smelled it.
I am not joking.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.501
-Did your editor say,
"Stop doing that"?

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.300
-Yes.
-"Stop doing it.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.067
You're scaring the buyers."

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:46.901
-They escorted me out before
the appetizer, and I was hungry.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.501
-Yeah, well, can I tell you

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.367
where I'm happiest
to see your name

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:53.400
is when I get an e-mail
from our talent department

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.200
saying Henry Winkler
is coming back on the show.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.400
-Thank you.
-It makes me so happy.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.567
What a joy it is
every single time you're here.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.701
You guys, that is Henry Winkler,
everybody.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.934
"Being Henry: The Fonz...
and Beyond" is available now.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:07.133
We'll be right back
with Brendan Hunt.

